  "description": "HackAaroh — The Open Source Sprint Code for Food Make meaningful contributions to open source, compete on the leaderboard, and get rewarded for the quality of your work. The Top 20 participants win Zomato gift cards. Website: https://hackaaroh-main.vercel.app/ How it works Connect your GitHub and join the sprint. Contribute to an open-source project. Your Pull Requests are tracked, including commits, changes, and merge status. Every contribution is evaluated out of 100: Code Quality & Design — 25 Technical Complexity — 25 Real-World Impact — 25 Testing & Reliability — 25 Scores are updated on the live leaderboard every day at 00:00 UTC. Rules Meaningful contributions are rewarded; spam and trivial PRs won't help your score. Rankings are based on the quality, difficulty, and impact of your contributions, not your commit count. PRs must follow the requirements of the project they are submitted to. Open-source projects across any tech stack are welcome, including React, Next.js, Bun, Rust, Linux, Tailwind, VS Code, and more.",
