    "details": "<h2>HackAaroh &mdash; The Open Source Sprint</h2>\n<p><strong>Code for Food</strong></p>\n<p>Make meaningful contributions to open source, compete on the leaderboard, and get rewarded for the quality of your work. <strong>The Top 20 participants win Zomato gift cards.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Website:</strong> <a href=\"https://hackaaroh-main.vercel.app/\">https://hackaaroh-main.vercel.app/</a></p>\n<h2>How it works</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Connect your GitHub and join the sprint.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Contribute to an open-source project.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Your Pull Requests are tracked, including commits, changes, and merge status.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Every contribution is evaluated out of 100:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Code Quality &amp; Design</strong> &mdash; 25</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Technical Complexity</strong> &mdash; 25</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Real-World Impact</strong> &mdash; 25</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Testing &amp; Reliability</strong> &mdash; 25</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Scores are updated on the live leaderboard every day at 00:00 UTC.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Rules</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Meaningful contributions are rewarded; spam and trivial PRs won't help your score.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Rankings are based on the quality, difficulty, and impact of your contributions, not your commit count.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>PRs must follow the requirements of the project they are submitted to.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Open-source projects across any tech stack are welcome, including React, Next.js, Bun, Rust, Linux, Tailwind, VS Code, and more.</p>",
